DESCRIPTION:Toronto&#x27\;s signature showcase of rising 2SLGBTQIA+ and wo
 men comedians\, anchored by 2 professional headliners! Babes! Come check o
 ut the comedy show highlighting the best new comedians Toronto has to offe
 r! This show is a comfortable\, welcoming space for fem\, women\, and/ or 
 queer comedians within their first couple of years in the industry to perf
 orm in front of a fun and welcoming audience! Featuring: Cameron Whittle G
 abriella Salon Dylan Paisley Youssef Kamar Mani Headlined by: Nile Seguin 
 Bita Joudaki Doors 7 45 pm\, show promptly at 8 pm (yes\, we actually star
 t on time!) Tickets are $12 but all are welcome regardless of means - DM @
 annasebastiencomedy on Instagram for Pay What You Can tickets. Check out a
  fresh line up of 5 new funny babes and 2 pro headliners the first Thursda
 y of each and every month\, produced and hosted by Anna Sebastien (@annase
 bastiencomedy). Hope to see you there! --- The venue: The show takes place
  in the theatre space in the downstairs area of Tallboys. Take a left when
  you walk in and head downstairs! The venue unfortunately has a few barrie
 rs to access. There is a large step to enter the main bar area. The theatr
 e space and washrooms are located down a staircase\, with tight corners fr
 om the bottom landing to the theatre. There is also a single step from the
  basement hallway into the venue room. Once inside\, there is no grade cha
 nge. There is a communal gender neutral washroom with urinals and toilets\
 , a singe stall unmarked gender neutral washroom with a toilet\, and a wom
 an&#x27\;s washroom with toilets. Seating is self-assigned and the venue i
 s intimate\, so we recommend groups arrive early so they can grab seats to
 gether Community: All are welcome at this event\, including allies\, that 
 recognize this is a queer space where we are inclusive and respectful of o
 ne another\, and where oppressive behaviour won&#x27\;t fly At this show w
 e only speak to our own identities\, we don&#x27\;t punch down\, and isms\
 , phobias\, and aggressive crowd work will never be tolerated. The show is
  hosted and produced by a queer\, nonbinary comedian who takes this seriou
 sly AF\, and all the comedians agree to community guidelines. This show wi
 ll be fun filled and full of friendly queers\, and the audience and comedi
 an can make new friends and mix and mingle afterwards. If you are flying s
 olo\, are nervous\, or have any questions\, feel free to DM the host @anna
 sebastiencomedy on Instagram. This is all about community! We all want a s
 exy\, healthy time! If you are feeling sick\, please stay home! Refund req
 uests will be honoured up to 12 hours before the show. You are totally wel
 come to wear a mask\, and we&#x27\;d be stoked if you rapid tested before 
 the show. ‍
LOCATION:Tallboys Craft Beer House\, 838 Bloor Street West
