BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:When The Dead Are Kept From Us
DTSTART:20261117T190000
DTEND:20261117T190000
UID:27284a8bd2aa889de13f93e844fb460a@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:Queer Death Salon is a virtual community space for all 2SLGBTQ
 IA+ people to come together to discuss death\, dying and grief. How do we 
 honor our dead when they are kept from us? What happens to us when we are 
 denied our chance to mourn? Let&#x27\;s come together to learn about and p
 ractice building ritual for grief when we are othered. Colleen (ʻoia/they
 /them) of Death Doula Does will guide participants through practical skill
 s for honoring our mourning and grief in rituals when we have no body to h
 old. Colleen is a Kanaka Maoli\, Queer\, mutual aider\, community-oriented
  death doula. Supporting those dying\, caregivers for the dying\, and grie
 vers for over a decade\, their work focuses on art-based grief spaces\, qu
 eer end-of-life planning\, and teaching how to be with death. (FOR MORE IN
 FO SEE TICKET LINK PROVIDED)
LOCATION:Online\, online
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/when-the-dead-are-kept-from-us
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
