BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:DREAMHOUSE: A Fashion Show in Honour of Trans Day of Remembrance
DTSTART:20261120T190000
DTEND:20261120T190000
UID:e069e7aad7727cd1f7ea5977478b92e2@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:DREAMHOUSE is a costume design and voguing dance program for b
 allroom youth\, culminating in a live performance to commemorate Trans Day
  of Remembrance (TDOR). &quot\;DREAMHOUSE&quot\; is a play on the Barbie D
 oll Dreamhouse\, referencing both the house structure of ballroom and the 
 ballroom vernacular term &quot\;doll.&quot\; The &quot\;doll&quot\; of PRO
 TECT THE DOLLS comes from ballroom\, not &quot\;gay slang&quot\; or &quot\
 ;Gen Z internet speak\,&quot\; but from the Black trans women who are the 
 heart of ballroom. DREAMHOUSE is a powerful tool of trans activism and art
 istry\, using creative mentorship to spotlight ballroom talent as the epic
 entre of queer arts and culture. DREAMHOUSE is led by Toronto ballroom com
 munity leaders Charlotte Carbone\, Diséiye Thompson\, Solange Alexander\,
  and Ern In Motion\, who are also multi-disciplinary artists in their resp
 ective practices of costume design and dance performance. Designers: Disé
 iye Thompson\, Char Carbone\, Fae Mulan\, Karume Unbothered\, Arsyn Pink L
 ady\, Sakura Pink Lady\, Shaddoe Pink Lady\, Thryv Old Navy Performers: Er
 n In Motion\, Solange Alexander\, Jaemy Siriano\, Krackle Old Navy\, Nicky
  007\, Vita 007\, Chess 007\, Dymund Pink Lady ‍
LOCATION:Toronto PWA Foundation\, 163 Queen St E
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/dreamhouse-a-fashion-show-in-honour-of-tra
 ns-day-of-remembrance
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
